# End-user simplicity

The end user does not want complicated solutions. Keep the product unified.

- Default messenger path is `gen` / `send <hex> hello` / `inbox` / `open`. No required `--url`, `--router`, `--snode`, `--key`, or hop lists.
- `gen` saves identity under `~/.arqma/msg/identity`. `inbox` and `open` use it. `send bob=<hex>` remembers the name in `~/.arqma/msg/contacts`.
- `utils/arqma-stack` starts storage + router and writes one env file; `arqma-msg` reads it.
- Extra hops, swarm announce, replica URLs, and TTL are operator knobs. Do not put them in the first-line examples.
- Storage and router stay separate PIDs from `arqmad`, but that is an operator fact — not something the messenger user should assemble.
- Prefer one default behavior over new flags. Do not split UX across more binaries.
- Do not flip Pulse stage 3 or default `--arqnet-backend`.
